        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(swift): enforce current formatting and lint rules",
        "body": "Closes #103202\nRelated: #103098\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where local iOS builds and the macOS SwiftFormat CI lane could fail as soon as Homebrew supplied SwiftFormat 0.62.1, because newly default-enabled rules exposed formatting drift across otherwise untouched Swift files.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nApplies the current SwiftFormat rules repo-wide instead of disabling them, refactors the few lint-heavy surfaces into clearer bounded units, and makes all native lint lanes strict. SwiftFormat 0.62.1 and SwiftLint 0.65.0 are now checksum-pinned so local and CI results cannot drift with Homebrew bottle timing; generated protocol sources remain excluded.\n\nThe iOS/shared source list is generated recursively, Swabble shares the root formatter configuration, and macOS MLX changes now route through the same native pre-push checks.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended runtime behavior change. Contributors get deterministic, warning-free Swift formatting and lint results on iOS, macOS, MLX, shared packages, and Swabble; future formatter updates will produce an explicit version change instead of surprise CI drift.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm format:swift`: 0/263 macOS files, 0/23 MLX/Swabble files, and 0/274 iOS/shared files require formatting.\n- Exact former CI command: `swiftformat --lint apps/macos/Sources --config config/swiftformat --exclude '**/OpenClawProtocol,**/HostEnvSecurityPolicy.generated.swift'` — 0/263 files require formatting.\n- `pnpm lint:swift`: 0 violations in 264 macOS/MLX files, 22 Swabble files, and 274 iOS/shared files.\n- `pnpm ios:build`: succeeded locally; embedded SwiftFormat and strict SwiftLint phases both passed, with no compiler warnings or errors.\n- `swift build --package-path apps/macos --product OpenClaw --configuration release`: succeeded with no compiler warnings or errors.\n- Focused iOS simulator run: 253 tests passed across gateway connection/security, node invocation, typography, and root-tab source guards; no compiler warnings or errors.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kx4zes3s9p30cszremarktcb`: `src/scripts/ci-changed-scope.test.ts` passed 30/30 tests.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: no actionable findings.\n",
